{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "experimentalDecorators": true,
    "useDefineForClassFields": false,
    "module": "ESNext",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "types": [],

    /* Bundler mode */
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,

    /* Linting */
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true

    /* Two further strictness flags are deliberately NOT enabled. Measured
       against this tree on 2026-08-01 (`tighten-type-checking`); the rule is to
       adopt a flag on the evidence of what it costs and buys here, never from a
       generic strictness checklist.

       noUncheckedIndexedAccess — 9,028 errors, concentrated in the solvers
         (dominosa 195, loopy 194, grid-geometry 150, rect 133). It applies to
         Int32Array as well as plain arrays, and typed arrays are this repo's
         deliberate house pattern for game state and render cache keys. Where an
         index is derived from the loop bounds immediately above it, the flag
         reports an impossibility whose only available fix is `!` at every
         access: no runtime safety, and arithmetic that is harder to read. Where
         the guarantee IS earned — parsing a game ID, a description, or a saved
         game — use a checked accessor at that boundary instead.

       exactOptionalPropertyTypes — 108 errors across 51 files. At nearly every
         site the honest fix is to widen `x?: T` to `x?: T | undefined`, which
         restores exactly the semantics already in force, so the churn buys
         documentation rather than correctness. No site was found where
         absent-versus-present-undefined is load-bearing: the two
         persistence-adjacent cases (store/settings.ts, store/saved-games.ts)
         round-trip identically either way. Worth revisiting if a future format
         ever distinguishes a missing key from an explicit null. */
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
